                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "efeb70ba-1c64-4a06-84e8-7f3bc1b4c5d5",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f3d2bcc-1b73-31a1-971d-5ffd4c0fd49f",
                        "source_sense_id": "d8bfd59e-8bab-3f32-b242-66855c993ff0",
                        "target_lang_word": "picturesquely",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "picturesquely",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d49c0d3-5b6f-32ee-9f16-7f6b21404412",
                                        "entry_id": "1775c7a9-a720-382f-be48-3e57d5808340",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a picturesque manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8f4b6eb-9c98-4de4-afa2-3333ece11a79",
                                                "sense_id": "8d49c0d3-5b6f-32ee-9f16-7f6b21404412",
                                                "text": "The red-painted farm-houses, peculiar to Norway, lay picturesquely scattered on the higher points of the undulating valley, where men and women were busy hay-making."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc53a1df-5ade-4dbe-94a3-9f472a3c51d8",
                                                "sense_id": "8d49c0d3-5b6f-32ee-9f16-7f6b21404412",
                                                "text": "An athlete might picturesquely lament that his ankle had betrayed him or that his wrist had gone on strike; and if such modes of speech acquired a wide vogue, we might now and then fall into the trap of supposing that we and our limbs are related in the way in which employers are related to their employees. We might start to talk seriously of cricketers being well advised to dismiss their limbs and to try to get on without them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc5716d7-bbf1-4b0c-a187-0a1f0192757b",
                                                "sense_id": "8d49c0d3-5b6f-32ee-9f16-7f6b21404412",
                                                "text": "Georgian and Regency houses cluster picturesquely around the sloping village green, which in springtime is carpeted with daffodils."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9da42a5b-ab07-4f10-81bb-c5a2680cbf08",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f3d2bcc-1b73-31a1-971d-5ffd4c0fd49f",
                        "source_sense_id": "d8bfd59e-8bab-3f32-b242-66855c993ff0",
                        "target_lang_word": "vividly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vividly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                        "entry_id": "7abacc78-af82-38d0-90a9-b3f0e24d83c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a vivid manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2961c25-eb2a-4c3f-a8e6-af65e808a116",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "Here, in the transept and choir, where the service was being held, one was conscious every moment of an increasing brightness; colours glowing vividly beneath the circular chandeliers, and the rows of small lights on the choristers' desks flashed and sparkled in front of the boys' faces, deep linen collars, and red neckbands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "084e1a3b-3104-4b6a-81d4-685a6cedda22",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "The water-level route, the whistle and the loud staccato exhaust of this great engine recalled most vividly memories of the New York Central Hudsons highballing along the Hudson River between Harmon and Albany!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84dbc8f-c541-4402-aa00-73fc0a812d13",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "The Campbell family’s fascination with white supremacy was vividly expressed in the names of Adolf’s two siblings, “Honszlynn Hinler Jeannie Campbell,” an homage to Heinrich Himmler, and “JoyceLynn Aryan Nation Campbell.”² In selecting their children’s peculiar names, the Campbells had exercised a right specifically recognized in New Jersey statutory law, which states, “The designation of a child’s name including the surname is the right of the child’s parent(s).”³"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
